<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5233" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bestĭa</span></b> , ae,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a cognomen in the Calpurnian family.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The consul</i> L. Calpurnius Bestia, <i><span class="en">Sall.
				J. 27, 4 al.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Flor. 3, 1,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The tribune of the people</i> L. Bestia, <i><span class="en">Cic. Brut.
				34, 128</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. de Or. 2, 70,
			283</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			Another <i>tribune of the people</i>, L. Bestia, <i>a confederate of Catiline</i>, <i><span class="en">Sall. C.
				17, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">43,
			1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
